            <ArticleTitle>[From disability to the adunatos: some thoughts on disability and somatoform pain disorder].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>365-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Disability, especially if related to a psychiatric disorder, such as somatoform pain disorder, is characterized by medical, psychological, relational, social and societal, as well as financial and political aspects. This manuscript, part of a PhD thesis which reflects on a possible dialogue between an ancient text and the modern conceptualization of disability, tries to address the phenomenological, historical and political dimensions of disability.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
